# -mavx2 (@MAVX2_FLAG@) is carried in PKG_CXXFLAGS via a configure-substituted
# placeholder. WRE §1.2.1 / R CMD check rationale (tools:::.check_make_vars):
#   * The "uflags" sub-check flags any mutation of the user CXXFLAGS variable
#     (value != "-o /dev/null"), so the package must NOT append to CXXFLAGS.
#   * The "pflags" sub-check greps the *.in* file (paths[1L] = Makevars.in) for
#     non-portable tokens; it sees the opaque "@MAVX2_FLAG@" placeholder, not the
#     literal "-mavx2", so PKG_CXXFLAGS in the SHIPPED Makevars.in is clean.
# -mavx2 is load-bearing: the _mm256_* intrinsics in lbw_math.hpp fail to compile
# without it, and the only AVX2 code is preprocessor-gated behind LBW_HAS_GLIBC_MVEC
# (set by the same configure AVX2 feature-test), so @MAVX2_FLAG@ is empty on
# non-AVX2 / non-x86 compilers and the intrinsics are not compiled there.
# -O3 is intentionally NOT set: R supplies the user/site -O level via $(CXXFLAGS)
# in $(ALL_CXXFLAGS); a user wanting -O3 sets it in ~/.R/Makevars. WRE: "flags
# such as -O2 ... are all specific to GCC" — packages must not hard-code them.
PKG_CXXFLAGS = @CXXFLAGS_STD@ @OMP_FLAGS@ @SIMD_FLAGS@ @MAVX2_FLAG@ -I. -DSTRICT_R_HEADERS
PKG_LIBS = @MVEC_LIBS@ $(LAPACK_LIBS) $(BLAS_LIBS) $(FLIBS)
PKG_SOURCES = c_api.cpp logit.cpp oris.cpp oris_trajectory.cpp oris_finalize.cpp cell_table.cpp r_bridge.cpp calib_validate.cpp sinkhorn.cpp calib_linalg.cpp greg.cpp chebyshev.cpp greenkhorn.cpp logit_calib.cpp newton_calib.cpp design_effect.cpp validation.cpp
